menu "Keepsake updates"

    config KEEPSAKE_OTA_ENABLED
        bool "Check for updates on GitHub Releases"
        default y
        help
            Once a day (and from Settings -> About), fetch the latest release's manifest and,
            if it is newer, download the image into the other app slot. See #40 and the
            release how-to in docs/guide.md.

    config KEEPSAKE_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
        string "Release manifest URL"
        depends on KEEPSAKE_OTA_ENABLED
        default "https://github.com/ekhumbata/keepsake/releases/latest/download/latest.json"
        help
            The small JSON file each release publishes (tools/release/make_manifest.py). The
            "latest" link always points at the newest non-prerelease release.

    config KEEPSAKE_OTA_CHECK_INTERVAL_HOURS
        int "Background check interval (hours)"
        depends on KEEPSAKE_OTA_ENABLED
        range 1 168
        default 24

    config KEEPSAKE_OTA_HEALTH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
        int "Health check timeout after an update (seconds)"
        range 30 600
        default 90
        help
            A new firmware has this long to reach Home with a working display (and the SD
            card, if it was mounted before the update) and keep running for 20 s. If it
            doesn't, the device goes back to the previous firmware.

endmenu
